<title>GERMANY: Degussa seeks sharp profit rise by 1998/99.</title>
<headline>Degussa seeks sharp profit rise by 1998/99.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>German chemicals and metals group Degussa AG said on Tuesday that it was aiming to boost its pretax profit to 800 million marks ($525.9 million) by its 1998/1999 business year.</p>
<p>In the 1994/1995 year, Degussa posted a pretax profit of 404 million marks.</p>
<p>Chief executive Uwe-Ernst Bufe told a news conference the earnings rise was needed to boost its return on equity to 15 percent after tax.</p>
<p>Degussa's business year runs to September 30.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525 ($ = 1.521 German Marks)</p>
